---
/* WHAT THIS SITE ACTUALLY DOES, NOT WHAT A TEMPLATE SAYS SITES DO.
 *
 * Most privacy policies are copied from a generator and describe a site the
 * author never built: cookies nobody sets, analytics nobody installed, a
 * "data controller" for a service with no accounts. That is a false statement
 * about yourself, published on your own site, and it is exactly the genre of
 * error this project exists to object to elsewhere.
 *
 * So every claim below was checked against the source before it was written:
 *
 *   no analytics        no gtag/plausible/fathom/posthog/segment, and no
 *                       third-party <script src> anywhere in src/
 *   no cookies          document.cookie appears nowhere
 *   one storage key     src/ui/units.mjs, localStorage 'units', metric or
 *                       imperial, and nothing else
 *   no server           output: 'static'; 63 prerendered files on Cloudflare
 *                       Workers static assets, no request-time code at all
 *   no accounts         nothing to sign into, no form that posts anywhere
 *   trip data in URL    /check keeps state in the query string, read and
 *                       written in the browser; it is never sent to us,
 *                       because there is no us to send it to
 *
 * If any of those stops being true, this page is wrong the same day. The
 * honest ones to watch are analytics and the affiliate programme.
 *
 * NOT WRITTEN BY A LAWYER, and it says so at the foot rather than pretending
 * otherwise. Frank: "They can be imperfect for the moment."
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const UPDATED = 'September 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy — Sizer"
  description="What Sizer collects, which is almost nothing, and why that is a consequence of how it is built."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-page px-6">

    <section class="pt-12 pb-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-lg text-ink-2">
        Sizer has no accounts, no analytics and no cookies. That is not a
        policy decision we might quietly reverse — it is a consequence of the
        site being a set of static files with no server to receive anything.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Last updated {UPDATED}.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">What we collect</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        Nothing. There is no sign-up, no newsletter, no contact form, and no
        code on this site that transmits anything about you anywhere.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">What your browser stores</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        One value, under the key <code class="rounded bg-surface-2 px-1">units</code>:
        whether you chose metric or imperial. It stays in your browser, it is
        never sent to us, and clearing your site data removes it.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        We set no cookies of any kind.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">The trip you type in</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        The trip checker runs entirely in your browser. Your flights, fares and
        bags are kept in the page's own address so the "copy link" button
        produces something that actually works — which means the answer you see
        is computed on your machine, from data already downloaded, and never
        reaches us.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        Worth knowing: because the trip lives in the URL, anyone you send that
        link to can see the same flights and bags. That is the point of it, but
        it is your call who gets the link.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">What our host sees</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        The site is served by Cloudflare, which handles the request and keeps
        its own operational logs — typically including IP address, time, and
        the page requested — for security and reliability. We do not add
        anything to those logs, and we do not use them to build any profile of
        you.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        That processing is Cloudflare's, under Cloudflare's terms, and is not
        something this site controls.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Links out</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        We link to airline baggage pages, manufacturer product pages and the
        occasional review, because a figure you cannot trace is not worth
        printing. Once you follow one of those links you are on someone else's
        site, under their privacy practices, not ours.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        There are currently no advertising, sponsorship or affiliate links on
        this site.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">If this changes</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ink-2">
        If analytics or an affiliate programme is ever added, this page changes
        on the same day, and the date at the top changes with it. We would
        rather say so plainly than let a stale page quietly become untrue.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="max-w-3xl border-t border-rule py-8 text-sm text-muted">
      This is an early draft written by the site's author, not by a lawyer, and
      it is not legal advice. It describes what the site does today as
      accurately as we can state it.
    </p>

  </div>
</Base>
